  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a clean, interpretable performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses a fast linear encoder (PCA), avoids image processing and aggregation complexity, and isolates the RNA signal alone. This gives a low-variance reference point against which every subsequent design choice (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion strategy) can be measured. It is also the cheapest experiment to run, preserving budget for more informative follow-ups. Once I have this RNA-only baseline, the next logical step is an image-only baseline (config_010) and then a simple multimodal config (config_016) to directly test whether and how much the image modality adds value."
}

